Added a retry helper with jittered backoff:

```ts
export async function withRetry<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>, attempts = 3): Promise<T> {
  for (let i = 0; ; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); }
    catch (err) { if (i >= attempts - 1) throw err; await sleep(2 ** i * 100 + Math.random() * 50); }
  }
}
```

The GitHub client now wraps its calls in it.
